      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessActor" name="Skills Training" id="id-c6f00a468c8346a488cb561aeea1d73f">
        <documentation>Sarah Collins&#xD;
&#xD;
https://skgov.sharepoint.com/:b:/r/sites/ICT/EOG/Shared%20Documents/Branch%20Orientation%20-%20Skills%20Training%20Branch%20-%202022.pdf?csf=1&amp;web=1&amp;e=h52xqm&#xD;
&#xD;
Purpose:&#xD;
The Skills Training Branch (STB) provides strategic direction and oversight for Saskatchewan’s training system, ensuring skills training programs align with employer business needs now and for the future. We do this by providing access to essential, technical and skilled trades training.&#xD;
&#xD;
Who do we serve?&#xD;
The STB provides program investments designed to address labour market needs of employers and the economic priorities of the Government of Saskatchewan.&#xD;
&#xD;
STB Key Programs and Service areas&#xD;
+ &lt;Essential Skills programs> encompasses a suite of non-credit and credit Adult  Basic Education programs for adult learners. This includes the Skills for Success  project.&#xD;
+ &lt;Skills Training programs> address the training needs of Saskatchewan business and industry to support labour market demand and to promote equity participation in training delivery.&#xD;
+ The &lt;Apprenticeship program> delivered through Saskatchewan Apprenticeship Trades and Certification Commission provides demand driven technical training to ensure skilled workers are available to meet Saskatchewan's labour market demand.&#xD;
+ The &lt;Canada-Saskatchewan Job Grant (CSJG)> is an employer-driven program that helps businesses and non-profit organizations train employees for available jobs and provide more opportunities for unemployed and underemployed workers to receive training.&#xD;
&#xD;
</documentation>
        <property key="number_employees" value="14"/>
        <property key="org_level" value="Branch"/>
        <property key="category" value="Department"/>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessActor" name="Training and Employment Services" id="id-619d35282bea46439c197f0cb07fc233">
        <documentation>ADM: Darcy Smycniuk&#xD;
&#xD;
The Training and Employer Services Division (TES) is responsible for training and other workforce solutions to develop, recruit, and retain a skilled and diverse workforce. TES helps Saskatchewan employers navigate their labour market options, and provide strategic direction, oversight and investment to align the Saskatchewan training system with labour market needs.</documentation>
        <property key="number_employees" value="131"/>
        <property key="category" value="Department"/>
        <property key="org_level" value="Division"/>
      </element>
